## Why This Is Asked

This ensures scalable, fair CKNE-driven caching across many tenants, balancing latency and hit rate in real time.

## Key Concepts

- CKNE-to-quota mapping with a guaranteed baseline
- CKNE-aware eviction policy (weighted LFU/LRU) plus selective prefetch
- Minute-by-minute rebalancing with safety guards and observability

## Code Example

```javascript
function computeQuotas(totSlots, tenants){
  const total = tenants.reduce((s,t)=>s+t.ckne,0);
  return tenants.map(t=>{
    const w = Math.max(0.05, t.ckne);
    const q = Math.max(1, Math.round((w/total)*totSlots));
    return {tenant: t.tenant, quota: q};
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle sudden CKNE spikes or missing data?
- What metrics confirm SLA while maintaining fairness?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world BI workloads multiplex dozens to thousands of tenants; CKNE-driven concurrency and memory control is critical for SLOs and fair sharing.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-resource mapping: concurrency, memory budget, spill/IO throttling
- Per-tenant quotas and dynamic reallocation cadence
- Fairness guarantees and explicit preemption rules
- Telemetry hooks and feedback for regret-free adjustment

## Code Example
```javascript
function allocate(tenants){
  // normalize CKNE 0-1 to weight, compute quotas
  const total = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ t.alloc = t.ckne/total; });
  return tenants;
}
```

